      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Lolo,_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Lolo Trail, a rugged path over the Bitterroot Mountains, was a vital hunting and trade corridor for the Salish, Kootenai, and Nez Perce long before settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Lolo,_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lolo’s name may stem from French fur trapper Lawrence Rence, or from “Le Louis,” the French name for Meriwether Lewis, reflecting early trade ties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
